{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>A vine-branch.</b> A vine-tendril, and a cluster of grapes hung upon it." "<b>And they bore it on a pole between two.</b> From the fact that it says ״וַיִּשָּׂאֻהוּ בַמּוֹט״ — do I not know it was between two? What does ״בִּשְׁנָיִם״ tell me? On two poles. How so? Eight carried the cluster, one carried a fig and one a pomegranate; Yehoshua and Kalev took nothing, because they were entirely intent on bringing an evil report — just as its fruit is extraordinary, so are its people extraordinary. And if you wish to know how much was one man's load, go and learn from the stones they set up at Gilgal — ״they lifted for themselves each man one stone from the Jordan onto his shoulder and set it up at Gilgal״ (Joshua 4) — and our Sages weighed them: the weight of each was forty se'ah. And it is a tradition: the load a man carries on his shoulders is only one third of the load that others help him lift (Sotah 34)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:44.192769494Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}